<article class="env-proposition" id="2FB8A7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/2FB8A7">Proposition <span data-tag="2FB8A7">7.2.2.4</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-category, and let $U_{\bullet }$ be a simplicial object of $\calX $. Then $U_{\bullet }$ is a group object of $\calX $ if and only if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The object $U_0$ is final in $\calX $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every decomposition $[n] = S \cup S'$, where $S \cap S' = \{ s\} $, the maps 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  U(S) \leftarrow U_ n \rightarrow U(S') \]
</div>
<p>
 exhibit $U_ n$ as a product of $U(S)$ and $U(S)$ in $\calX $. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from characterization $(4'')$ of Proposition <a href="/tag/9B195B" data-tag="9B195B">6.1.2.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>